:false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-06T16:05:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T16:36:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.6.1 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Radeon RX 560 Series (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21912.14) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-4570 CPU @ 3.20GHz (4 threads) - 15.93 ГиБ memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I go into the import settings when opening an `.fbx` file and enable skipping certain nodes, such as a light source or camera, the output displays errors:\n```\nERROR: Node not found: \"Camera\" (relative to \"Node3D\").\nERROR: Node not found: \"Light\" (relative to \"Node3D\").\n```\n\n<img width=\"1019\" height=\"270\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83c68163-f9ad-4805-8d50-3dd5d8bcd034\" />\n\nI also tested this with `GLB` files and didn't encounter this error, so I can confidently say it's `FBX`-specific.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the advanced import settings by double-clicking the .fbx file.\n2. Try skipping the import of some nodes, such as lighting or camera.\n3. Click Retry Import, and you'll see the errors.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25799220/MRP.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117150/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":n